{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0043220","isObsolete":false,"name":"Schmidt-Lanterman incisure","definition":{"text":"Regions within compact myelin in which the cytoplasmic faces of the enveloping myelin sheath are not tightly juxtaposed, and include cytoplasm from the cell responsible for making the myelin. Schmidt-Lanterman incisures occur in the compact myelin internode, while lateral loops are analogous structures found in the paranodal region adjacent to the nodes of Ranvier."},"synonyms":[{"name":"Schmidt-Lanterman cleft","type":"exact"}],"secondaryIds":["GO:0044287"],"history":[{"timestamp":"2026-07-02","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2026-07-02","action":"Deleted","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-03-22","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-03-22","action":"Deleted","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2024-03-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0110165 (cellular anatomical structure)"},{"timestamp":"2019-09-12","action":"Deleted","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0044464 (obsolete cell part)"},{"timestamp":"2010-12-23","action":"Updated","category":"TERM","text":"Schmidt-Lanterman incisure"},{"timestamp":"2010-12-23","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Regions within compact myelin in which the cytoplasmic faces of the enveloping myelin sheath are not tightly juxtaposed, and include cytoplasm from the cell responsible for making the myelin. Schmidt-Lanterman incisures occur in the compact myelin internode, while lateral loops are analogous structures found in the paranodal region adjacent to the nodes of Ranvier."},{"timestamp":"2010-12-23","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"Regions within compact myelin in which the cytoplasmic faces of the enveloping myelin sh